# The build context is only what the build needs: the package and its metadata, and the pinned
# requirements of nsz (the Dockerfile itself is read separately). Everything else
# (the website and its node_modules, the tests, the docs, .git) stays out, so the context is small
# and a change to a page does not invalidate the build cache.
*
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE
!warpzone
!docker/nsz-requirements.txt
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
